#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "balance_code"
msgid "Balance code"
msgstr "Código de saldo"

#. Redeem balance code: the server answered that this code was already redeemed. Distinct from invalid -- the user may have redeemed it on an earlier attempt that looked like a failure.
msgctxt "balance_code_already_redeemed_message"
msgid "This balance code has already been redeemed. If you redeemed it earlier, the data is already on your balance."
msgstr "Este código de saldo já foi resgatado. Se o resgatou antes, os dados já estão no seu saldo."

#. Redeem balance code: confirmation of the data a redeemed code added to the network's balance (amount is a formatted byte count, e.g. "5.00 GiB"). A balance code is data only: never a plan or Pro upgrade.
msgctxt "balance_code_data_added"
msgid "{} of data added to your balance."
msgstr "Foram adicionados {} de dados ao seu saldo."

#. Redeem balance code: the server answered and rejected the code as unknown/invalid. Distinct from a transport failure, which must never be reported as a bad code.
msgctxt "balance_code_invalid_message"
msgid "That balance code isn't valid. Check the code and try again."
msgstr "Esse código de saldo não é válido. Verifique o código e tente novamente."

#. Confirmation shown after a balance code is redeemed.
msgctxt "balance_code_redeemed"
msgid "Balance code redeemed."
msgstr "Código de saldo resgatado."

#. Redeem balance code: the request never got a server answer (network failure). Must NOT be worded as 'bad code' -- the redeem may have committed server-side, so tell the user to check their balance before retrying.
msgctxt "balance_code_transport_error"
msgid "We couldn't reach the server — check your connection. If you were charged, the code may already be applied; check your balance before trying again."
msgstr "Não conseguimos contactar o servidor — verifique a sua ligação. Se lhe foi cobrado, o código pode já ter sido aplicado; verifique o seu saldo antes de tentar novamente."

#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "balance_code_where_to_buy"
msgid "Don't have a code? Data codes can be purchased at ur.io and emailed to you."
msgstr "Não tem um código? Pode comprar códigos de dados em ur.io e recebê-los por e-mail."

#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "balance_codes_link"
msgid "Balance codes"
msgstr "Códigos de saldo"

#. Linux redeem-code sheet: shown in place of the redeemed-codes history when getNetworkRedeemedBalanceCodes FAILS (transport error, no response, or a server-side error) — distinct from the empty state's "No balance codes found", which is only for a successful fetch with no codes.
msgctxt "balance_codes_load_error"
msgid "Couldn't load your balance codes. Check your connection and try again."
msgstr "Não foi possível carregar os seus códigos de saldo. Verifique a sua ligação e tente novamente."

